          "grammarNotes": "TELLING TIME:\n• 'Che ore sono?' — What time is it? (literally 'what hours are they?')\n• 'È l'una.' — It's one o'clock. (singular — only for one!)\n• 'Sono le due / le tre / le dieci…' — It's two / three / ten o'clock. (plural: sono le + number)\n• 'Sono le tre e mezza.' — It's half past three.\n• 'Sono le otto meno dieci.' — It's ten to eight. (literally 'eight minus ten')\n\nTIMES OF DAY: la mattina → 'di mattina', il pomeriggio → 'di pomeriggio', la sera → 'di sera':\n'Vado al bar alle otto di mattina.' — I go to the bar at eight in the morning.\n\nPRICES with the verb costare (to cost):\n• 'Quanto costa?' — How much does it cost? (one thing)\n• 'Quanto costano?' — How much do they cost? (several things)\n• 'Il caffè costa un euro.' — The coffee costs one euro.\n• 'I cornetti costano quattro euro.' — The croissants cost four euros.\n\nEURO is invariable: un euro, due euro, cento euro — it never changes.",
