          ],
          "grammarNotes": "I PRONOMI DIRETTI — the little words that replace 'him / her / it / them'.\n\nTHE FOUR FORMS:\n• lo — him, it (m sing): 'Il film? Lo vedo domani.' — The film? I see it tomorrow.\n• la — her, it (f sing): 'La canzone? La ascolto.' — The song? I listen to it.\n• li — them (m pl): 'I libri? Li leggo.' — The books? I read them.\n• le — them (f pl): 'Le lettere? Le scrivo.' — The letters? I write them.\n\nPOSITION — before the verb, the opposite of English:\n'Lo conosci?' — Do you know HIM? (lo comes before conosci)\n'La vedo domani.' — I see HER tomorrow. 💛\n\nBEFORE A VOWEL, lo and la drop to l': 'L'ascolto.' — I listen to it. (Same l' rule as the articles, Unit 5.)\n\nWHY: Italians hate repeating nouns. 'Conosci Marco?' — 'Sì, lo conosco.' — Yes, I know HIM.\nThe pronoun carries the gender and number of what it replaces: lo for il ragazzo, la for la ragazza, li for i libri, le for le lettere.\n\n💛 'Lo conosci?' — Do you know him? 'La vedo domani.' — I'll see her tomorrow. 'La chiamo domani.' — I'll call her tomorrow.",
