        {
          "id": "u33l2",
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Mi, ti, gli, le — a chi?",
          "dictionaryRefs": [
            "mandare",
            "rispondere",
            "telefonare",
            "la-notizia",
            "il-messaggio",
            "la-foto",
            "il-numero",
            "domani",
            "subito"
          ],
          "grammarNotes": "I PRONOMI INDIRETTI — the little words for 'TO someone'. Unit 19 answered 'who/what?' (lo, la, li, le — I see HIM: lo vedo). This unit answers 'TO whom?':\n\n• mi — to me: 'Mi scrivi?' — Will you write to me?\n• ti — to you: 'Ti scrivo domani.' — I'll write to you tomorrow. 💛\n• gli — to him: 'Gli telefono.' — I'll phone him.\n• le — to her: 'Le mando un messaggio.' — I'll send her a message.\n• ci — to us: 'Ci scrivete?' — Will you write to us?\n• vi — to you (plural): 'Vi mando una foto.' — I'll send you (all) a photo.\n• loro — to them: goes AFTER the verb — 'Telefono loro domani.' (or, more common: 'Gli telefono domani.')\n\nPOSITION: before the verb, like the direct pronouns — ti scrivo, gli telefono, le mando.\n\nTHE CONTRAST (Unit 19 vs now):\n• 'La vedo domani.' — I see HER tomorrow. (direct: whom do I see? her)\n• 'Le scrivo domani.' — I write TO her tomorrow. (indirect: to whom? to her)\nSame person, different job. With vedere the person is the object; with scrivere/mandare/telefonare the person RECEIVES the action.\n\nVERBS THAT TAKE THE INDIRECT: scrivere a, mandare a, telefonare a, rispondere a, dare a (to give — later).",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "u33l2e1",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Complete the sentence. 💛 (I'll write to you tomorrow.)",
              "sentence": "___ scrivo domani.",
              "answers": [
                "Ti"
              ],
              "explanation": "'Ti scrivo domani.' — ti (to you) before the verb. 💛 The promise of the morning after.",
              "dictionaryRefs": [
                "scrivere",
                "domani"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "u33l2e2",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Complete the sentence. (I'll phone her tomorrow.)",
              "sentence": "___ telefono domani.",
              "answers": [
                "Le"
              ],
              "explanation": "'Le telefono domani.' — le (to her). Careful: la vedo (I see her, direct) vs le telefono (I phone her, indirect).",
              "dictionaryRefs": [
                "telefonare",
                "domani"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "u33l2e3",
