        {
          "id": "u34l2",
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Ci: là, di questa cosa, noi due",
          "dictionaryRefs": [
            "ci-vediamo",
            "pensare",
            "la-cosa",
            "stasera",
            "il-gelato",
            "il-bar",
            "il-cinema",
            "la-festa",
            "ce",
            "ci-sono"
          ],
          "grammarNotes": "CI — one syllable, three jobs. You already know two of its cousins: c'è / ci sono (Unit 4).\n\n1. CI = THERE — it replaces a place (a + place, in + place):\n'Vai al bar domani?' — 'Sì, ci vado domani.' — Yes, I'm going (there) tomorrow.\n'Conosci il museo?' — 'Sì, ci vado domani.' — Yes, I'm going (there) tomorrow.\n\n2. CI = ABOUT IT — with pensare and friends:\n'Ci penso io.' — I'll think about it. 'Ci pensi?' — Are you thinking about it?\n\n3. CI = EACH OTHER — the reflexive 'we':\n'Ci vediamo domani!' — See you tomorrow! (we see each other)\n'Ci sentiamo!' — Talk soon! (we hear each other — on the phone)\n\nC'È / CI SONO, REVIEW: 'Stasera c'è un film bello al cinema.' — Tonight there's a nice film at the cinema. 'Ci sono due cose.' — There are two things.\n\nWHY so small a word: Italian hates repeating places and topics. The answer to 'where/about what' collapses into ci before the verb.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "u34l2e1",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Complete the answer. (Are you going to the bar tomorrow? — Yes, I'm going there.) (Unit 5 recycling)",
              "sentence": "'Vai al bar domani?' — 'Sì, ___ vado domani.'",
              "answers": [
                "ci"
              ],
              "explanation": "'Sì, ci vado domani.' — ci replaces 'al bar': I'm going THERE. Before the verb, like the pronouns of Units 19/33.",
              "dictionaryRefs": [
                "il-bar",
                "andare",
                "domani"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "u34l2e2",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Complete the sentence. (I'll think about it.)",
              "sentence": "___ penso io.",
              "answers": [
                "Ci"
              ],
              "explanation": "'Ci penso io.' — ci (about it) + penso (pensare) + io for emphasis.",
              "dictionaryRefs": [
                "pensare"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "u34l2e3",
