          ],
          "grammarNotes": "AL TELEFONO — the register of calls and texts.\n\nON THE PHONE:\n• 'Pronto?' — Hello? (literally 'ready')\n• 'Chi parla?' — Who's speaking? — 'Sono Alex.' — It's Alex.\n• 'Non sento bene.' — I can't hear well.\n• 'Ti richiamo dopo.' — I'll call you back later.\n• 'Ci sentiamo domani!' — Talk tomorrow! (ci = each other, Unit 34)\n\nTEXTING — short, warm, present tense:\n• 'Ci sei?' — Are you around? (literally: are you there?)\n• 'A dopo!' — See you later! (Unit 30's dopo)\n• 💛 'Mi mandi l'indirizzo?' — Will you send me the address?\n\nPRONOUN CONSOLIDATION — all four little-word families in one place:\n• direct (Unit 19): 'Lo vedo domani.' — I see him tomorrow.\n• indirect (Unit 33): 'Gli scrivo domani.' — I write to him tomorrow.\n• ci, there/about it (Unit 34): 'Ci vado domani.' — I'm going there tomorrow.\n• ne, of them (Unit 35): 'Ne ho due.' — I have two of them.\n• and the phone's own: 'Ti richiamo.' — I'll call YOU back.\n\nSame position for all: before the verb. The question is always: what does the little word replace?",
